.TH SPINE 1 "April 2026" "Cacti" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spine \- High-speed poller for Cacti
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spine
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spine
is a high-performance, multi-threaded, and now asynchronous (libuv-based) poller for Cacti. It is designed to be much faster than the default cmd.php poller, capable of polling tens of thousands of hosts in just a few seconds.
.PP
The latest architecture features a truly non-blocking event loop, enabling extreme concurrency with minimal resource usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-conf\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Read configuration from \fIFILE\fR. Default is /etc/spine.conf.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR
Verify configuration and exit.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug logging.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-first\fR=\fIID\fR
Start polling at device \fIID\fR.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-last\fR=\fIID\fR
End polling at device \fIID\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-poller\fR=\fIID\fR
Set the poller \fIID\fR.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR=\fINUM\fR
Set the number of threads to use (overrides DB setting).
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-hostlist\fR=\fILIST\fR
Poll only the specified hosts (comma separated).
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-stdout\fR
Log to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-no-syslog\fR
Do not log to syslog.
.SH ASYNCHRONOUS FEATURES
.TP
\fBSmart SQL Batching\fR
Spine buffers SQL results and flushes them in large batches to the database. This significantly reduces the overhead on the MariaDB/MySQL server. The flush occurs when the buffer is full or every 500ms.
.TP
\fBNon-Blocking DNS (c-ares)\fR
Spine uses the c-ares library for truly asynchronous DNS resolution. This ensures that slow DNS servers do not block the polling cycle.
.TP
\fBTelemetry Socket\fR
A real-time observability socket (Unix Domain Socket) is available to export internal metrics like P99 latency and queue depth in JSON format.
.TP
\fBStage-Based Pipeline\fR
The polling engine is refactored into a SOLID pipeline (DNS -> Ping -> SNMP -> Flush), allowing for maximum extensibility and reliability.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/spine.conf\fR
Default configuration file location.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcacti\fR(1), \fBrrdtool\fR(1).
